From 903c48c1caff947cf58b4f43b0746d3c5803c244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:08:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/61] docs: ARMA, ARMA.optim, VAR and seas man pages match
 the code (TS-26)

Roxygen and Rd (NNS.VAR.Rd edited by hand because its committed Rd
already differs from roxygen output in other places):
- NNS.ARMA best.periods: default is 1, not [2].
- NNS.ARMA.optim: the default obj.fn is MSE divided by the degree-1
  co-partial-moment co-movement (not Spearman / SSE), objective defaults
  to "min" (not "max"), the description no longer says 'minimum sum
  of squared errors', and pred.int is built deterministically from the
  validation errors (UPM.VaR + |bias|), not with NNS.meboot.
- NNS.VAR multivariate: NNS.stack(method = 1, stack = FALSE) evaluated on
  the forecast-period lag rows (the code uses method = 1).
- NNS.seas: describe the no-seasonality sentinel row (Period 1, or 0 for
  fewer than 5 observations) instead of a 'No Seasonality Detected'
  string.
Documentation only.
